<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Midway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Midway · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Midway was a naval and air battle fought in June 1942 near Midway Atoll in the central Pacific during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> forces sank four Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aircraft-carrier">fleet carriers</a>, inflicting losses the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> could not replace. The battle is widely seen as the turning point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a>, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> was largely on the defensive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway.jpg" alt="Battle of Midway" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: USN, photographed from USS Pensacola (CA-24) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USS_Yorktown_(CV-5)_is_hit_by_a_torpedo_on_4_June_1942.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
